course: dictionary
lesson: 5241
title: Jiggle and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word jiggle can mean to move quickly with small movements, up and down or from side to side. It can also mean to shake something lightly, like a key in a stiff lock.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «Jiggle the key gently until the lock turns» shows a light shaking, not a big throw. «His leg began to jiggle under the table» shows quick, small movements, and the table tells you he may be nervous or impatient.
explain: Use the swap check. Try "shake it lightly" or "move quickly up and down" in the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: To jiggle means to move quickly with small movements, up and down or from side to side.
fact: Jiggle can be a verb (she jiggles, she jiggled) or a noun (a jiggle).
fact: To jiggle something can mean to shake it lightly, like a key in a stiff lock.
fact: «In a solid the particles are packed tightly and only jiggle in place, so a solid keeps its own shape.»
fact: «Atoms and the particles they make are never still: they jiggle, bump and drift.»
exercise: «She gave the stiff lock a gentle jiggle with her key.» What does jiggle mean here? | *To shake it lightly | To throw the key far away | To lose the key in the grass | To polish the key until it shines
exercise: «His leg began to jiggle under the table while he waited.» What does this suggest about him? | He is asleep | He is very cold and wet | He is singing a song | *He is nervous or impatient
exercise: «Jelly jiggles on the plate.» Which word in this sentence is the verb? | *Jiggles | On | Plate | Jelly
test: «The jelly jiggled when the bus stopped.» What does jiggled mean? | Broke into tiny pieces | Became very hot | *Moved quickly up and down or from side to side | Froze completely
test: Which word means nearly the same as jiggle when it means shaking something lightly? | Sing | *Shake | Smell | Sleep
exam: «Jiggle the handle gently, and the door may open.» What is the best meaning of jiggle here? | Sleep | Count how many times it turns | Paint it bright red | *Shake it lightly to free it | Leave it alone for a week
